---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout title="About George Choulakis">
  <main>
    <section class="container intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">about me</p>
      <h1>I like the part where the mess becomes a system.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        I’m George Choulakis. I work where data, automation, reporting, and business processes meet.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="container visual">
      <img src={`${base}illustrations/george-about.svg`} alt="Doodle scenes about George, databases, music, cats and rubber-duck debugging" />
    </section>

    <section class="container story">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What I do</h2>
        <p>
          Most of my work starts with something slightly uncomfortable: an Excel process that takes too long,
          data living in several systems, reports that people no longer fully trust, or a workflow that depends
          on too much manual effort.
        </p>
        <p>
          I enjoy tracing that problem back to its structure, then building something clearer: a data model,
          an integration, a reporting layer, an automated process, or simply a better way for people to understand what is happening.
        </p>

        <h2>How I think about technical work</h2>
        <p>
          A technically correct system can still be a bad system if nobody understands it, maintaining it is painful,
          or it quietly creates more work somewhere else. I care about the boring parts: naming, handovers, failure states,
          documentation, and whether the next person can reason about what was built.
        </p>

        <h2>And outside the database?</h2>
        <p>
          Music has been part of my life for years. I sing, play guitar, nearly always have white wired headphones nearby,
          and have a soft spot for cats, Playmobil figures, and rubber ducks with unexpectedly senior debugging responsibilities.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside>
        <div class="note">
          <span class="mono">CURRENT INTERESTS</span>
          <p>Data integration</p>
          <p>Reporting automation</p>
          <p>Business intelligence</p>
          <p>Internal tools</p>
          <p>Technical storytelling</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.intro { padding-top:75px; max-width:960px; margin-left:auto; margin-right:auto; }
h1 { font-size:clamp(3.3rem,7.5vw,7rem); line-height:.94; letter-spacing:-.06em; margin:18px 0 26px; }
.lead { color:var(--muted); font-size:1.25rem; max-width:760px; }
.visual { margin-top:58px; }
.visual img { width:100%; border:2px solid #111; border-radius:32px; box-shadow:7px 7px 0 #111; }
.story { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 260px; gap:80px; padding-top:85px; }
.note { position:sticky; top:25px; border:2px solid #111; padding:22px; border-radius:24px; background:#fff3c8; transform:rotate(1.5deg); box-shadow:4px 4px 0 #111; }
.note span { font-size:.7rem; }
.note p { margin:.75rem 0; font-weight:700; color:#3e454c; }
@media(max-width:800px){ .story{grid-template-columns:1fr;} .note{position:static;} }
</style>
